    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n90858" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρώην</span></b> , 
			Dor.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρώᾱν</span></b> 
		<i><span class="en">
			Theoc.
			5.4
		</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
			15.15
		</span></i>; 
			contr.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρῶν</span></b> 
		<i><span class="en">
			Call.
			<u>Fr.</u>
			84
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			Herod.
			5.62
		</span></i>; <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρᾶν</span></b> 
		<i><span class="en">
			Theoc.
			2.115
		</span></i>:—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>lately, just
				now</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				5.832
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				24.500
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				408
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Alex.
				258
			</span></i>, Herod.l.c., <i><span class="en">
				<u>UPZ</u>
				42.25
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(ii B.C.)</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Cic.
				<u>Att.</u>
				6.4.3
			</span></i>, etc.; in a book, <i>above</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>EN</u>
				1104b18
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>long ago</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Procop.Gaz.
				<u>Pan.</u>
				p.505
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				B.
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀγησίλαος ὁ π</span>. ib.<i><span class="en">
				p.514
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				B.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> more definitely, <i>the
				day before yesterday</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐ . . χθές,
				ἀλλὰ π</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				3.113
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μέχρι οὗ π. τε καὶ
			χθές</span> till yesterday or <i>the day before</i>, i.e. till
				<i>very lately</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				2.53
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. καὶ χθές</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					44.42
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χθές τε καὶ π</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ra.</u>
				726
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χθὲς καὶ π</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				677d
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ ἐχθὲς καὶ π</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Grg.</u>
				470d
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐχθὲς καὶ π</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Isoc.
				6.27
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄρτι καὶ π., ὀψὲ καὶ
			π</span>., <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Brut.</u>
				1
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				2.394b
			</span></i>. (The first syll. of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρώαν</span>
			is short in <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
			</span></i> ll.cc.; <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρόαν</span></b>  is
			written in <i><span class="en">
				15.15
			</span></i> (codd. opt.), v.l. in
			<i><span class="en">
				4.60
			</span></i>.)</div>
